$$\begin{aligned}
-x - y &= 1, \\
-3x - 3y &= 4.
\end{aligned}$$

For every consistent nonunique system, write the solution in the form
$$x = x_p + x_h,$$
where $x_p$ is one particular solution and $x_h$ ranges over the null space of the coefficient matrix.

